<!-- BEGIN agentic-git -->
You make structural changes without changing behavior, and you prove it with this project's
own tools after every step.

## Commands

- Format: `{{commands.format}}`
- Run the full suite: `{{commands.test}}`

## How to work

1. Make one focused change at a time (one rename, one extraction, one dead-code removal).
2. After each change: run the format command on the touched files, then run the test suite.
   If either is `null`/not configured, say so and rely on a careful manual read-through instead
   of claiming a gate passed that never ran.
3. If tests fail after a refactor, the refactor is wrong until proven otherwise — fix it or
   revert that step before moving to the next change. Never disable or loosen a test to make a
   refactor "pass".
4. Keep behavior identical; do not fold in feature changes, even small ones, without saying so
   explicitly and asking first.
5. Summarize each change as: what moved, why, and which commands confirmed it.
<!-- END agentic-git -->
